[Optimal Approach] Using Mathematical Formula – O(1) Time and O(1) SpaceThe arrangements attacks where knight to move 2 steps in the horizontal direction and 1 step in the vertical. to 4 * (n - 2) * (m - 1) and similarly for 2 steps in the vertical direction and 1 step in the horizontal. Thus the answer will be Total possible arrangement - 4 * (n - 2) * (m - 1) - 4 * (n - 1) * (m - 2) which is (n*m)*(n*m - 1) - 4 * (n - 2) * (m - 1) - 4 * (n - 1) * (m - 2)How does this work?Consider  knight to move 2 steps in the horizontal direction and 1 step in the  vertical. So if we are at (i, j) after such moves we can reach at (i+2,  j+1), (i+2, j-1), (i-2, j+1), (i-2, j-1). To have (i+2) inside the board  we can have our positions 0 to n-3 i.e we have to leave the last two  rows otherwise (i+2) will be out of the board. similarly for (i-2) range  is possible if 2 to n-1.Similarly for (j+1) range will be 0 to m-2, and for (j-1) range will be 1 to m-1 i.e one column less in each case.So, arrangements in this case where attack possible equal to 4 * (n - 2) * (m - 1)Similarly,  if we consider two steps in vertical and one step in horizontal we will  have one less row and two less col so that two knights can attack each  other. We subtract this arrangement from total arrangements which is m * n * (n * n - 1). Hence the answer will be m * n * (m * n - 1) - 4 * (n - 2) * (m - 1) - 4 * (n - 1) * (m - 2)
